    {
      "id": "claim_ad2f7bb18fa24f498ff472819b7b64f4",
      "statement": "setStoredWalletAddress writes to the dedicated wallet MMKV instance (keys wallet_address and wallet_revision) with two invariants: it no-ops when the address is unchanged so the revision only moves on real transitions, and it writes the incremented revision before the address write/removal so value-changed listeners always read a complete, self-consistent { address, revision } snapshot; the revision increments on every connect, switch, and disconnect, making a reconnect of the same address a new session.",
      "evidence": [
